---
import CodeBlock from '../../../components/CodeBlock.astro'
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'

const reproduce = `python3 scripts/verify-native-macos-recording.py \\
  --installation '/path/to/relocated installation' \\
  --output /new/output/dir --format mp4 \\
  --duration-ms 120000 --case 1920x1080@120:audio --load-workers 5 \\
  --required-distinct-fps 120 --require-no-recorder-drops --require-native-capture \\
  --require-source-continuity`
---

<DocsLayout
  title="Performance"
  description="Measured native CEF 156 capture throughput, with host, workload and reproduction command."
  section="performance"
>
  <h1>Performance</h1>
  <p>
    Latest valid measurements for the CEF 156 engine. Each result names its commit, host and
    workload. The full record, including earlier runs and limits, is in
    <a href="https://github.com/skyaara/suitecut/blob/main/docs/benchmarks.md">docs/benchmarks.md</a
    >.
  </p>
  <h2 id="macos-recording">1080p120 recording on macOS</h2>
  <p>
    Measured 2026-10-23 at commit <code>4694aa1</code> on an Apple M4 (16 GB, macOS 27.0.1). IOSurface
    capture, Metal NV12 conversion and <code>h264_videotoolbox</code> MP4, with 48 kHz page audio, the
    per-frame canvas-reallocation fixture and five CPU load workers.
  </p>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Run</th>
        <th>Distinct FPS</th>
        <th>Held paints</th>
        <th>Audio</th>
        <th>Load average</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>120 s</td>
        <td>119.07</td>
        <td>112 (0.78%)</td>
        <td>no silence</td>
        <td>3.9–8.4</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>60 s</td>
        <td>119.25</td>
        <td>45 (0.62%)</td>
        <td>no silence</td>
        <td>8.0–11.4</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>10 s, A/V sync</td>
        <td>120.00</td>
        <td>0</td>
        <td>8.33 ms audio delay</td>
        <td>9.6–10.2</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>
    The recorder dropped and coalesced no frames; held paints are frames CEF never delivered. The
    strict sustained 120 FPS gate did not pass on the longer runs on this busy host. An earlier run
    of the same command on 2026-10-20, before the runtime modularization and on a quieter host,
    measured 120.00 distinct FPS over 120 s with no held paints.
  </p>
  <h2 id="reproduce">Reproduce</h2>
  <CodeBlock label="Terminal" code={reproduce} />
  <p>
    Build and relocate the runtime with the macOS full-runtime guide first. Add
    <code>--audio-sync-proof</code> for the A/V sync row, and state the fixture mode with any number you
    publish.
  </p>
  <h2 id="limits">Limits</h2>
  <p>
    macOS ARM64 only. Arbitrary page workloads, popup paths and live streaming throughput are not
    covered. A 120 FPS container can still repeat images that CEF never delivered under contention.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
